  "purpose": "Deterministic calibration corpus for the TVM v2 value parser. Stage contract: raw span -> parsed canonical representation -> evidence verification. No LLM is used as a judge at any stage (operator directive Step 3).",
  "ground_truth_authority": "The expected classifications for the DIRECTIVE_EXEMPLAR cases are derived from the operator directive's own exemplar list and category taxonomy (POINT / RANGE / INEQUALITY / ORDINAL_QUALITATIVE / NOT_NUMERIC). The EXTENDED and MALFORMED cases are authored from the pre-specified ruleset (NORMALIZATION_RULES.json), which was specified BEFORE the parser implementation was written. Ground truths are NOT derived from the parser's own behavior (Constitution Article VIII).",
  "corpus_immutability_rule": "Disagreement between the parser and this corpus is a parser defect, never a corpus defect. This corpus may not be edited after the parser runs against it; its sha256 is pinned in tests/test_r412_tvm_v2.py and in R412_GRADIENT_V2_PREREGISTRATION.json. Any corpus change requires a new corpus version and a new preregistration.",
  "field_context_note": "VALUE and YEAR are distinct parse contexts, resolved by the caller's explicit field declaration (never by heuristic guessing and never by an LLM). Case C031 demonstrates: the same span '2023' is a POINT value in VALUE context and a YEAR in YEAR context.",
